BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 606.20 Td (Linked Lists are dynamic data structures that store values in non-contiguous memory called nodes. Each node) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 592.80 Td (refers to the other using memory pointers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 572.90 Td (Linked lists are wonderful data structures that let us build without needing to estimate how much memory will be) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 559.50 Td (needed upfront.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 539.60 Td (Arrays let us randomly access any element quickly, but insertion and deletion is slow because elements need to) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 526.20 Td (shift to make room or close the gap.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 506.30 Td (And Linked List came in to solve the weakness of arrays - Linked lists make inserting and deleting fast once we) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 492.90 Td (have reached the right spot, but getting to that spot is slow because there's no random access.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 473.00 Td (Drawbacks of general linked lists:) Tj ET
