BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 346.15 Td (Skip lists are a probabilistic data structure constructed from several layers of linked lists. It is called as) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 332.75 Td (probabilistic data structure because it uses random coin flips to build itself.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 312.85 Td (The bottom layer is just a regular sorted linked list connecting an ordered sequence of elements.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 292.95 Td (Each new layer above removes some elements from the underlying layer \(based on a fixed probability\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 279.55 Td (producing a sparser version of the layer below.) Tj ET
